From 713ec69d0d6a885e6775861b4acf9d977dca0c02 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 09:11:43 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09159/11362] Fire counters: a lever that never runs must not
 be recorded as a lever that failed

REQ-ARC-BENCH-6270. The reachability guard proves a flag's code is LOADED. It
cannot prove the code RUNS, and the first scored-engine A/B walked straight into
that gap.

CARNOT_ARC_HAZARD_MOVE_PRUNER returned baseline and arm sweeps identical to the
digit -- 16 levels, 48,313 actions, both arms. "HOLD: no level gained" would have
been recorded, reading as "measured, does not help." Measured directly on tu93
with the flag set: flag_resolved True, observe_calls 292, observed_nav_transitions
288, model_fitted FALSE, rows_pruned 0. The lever is wired and running. The
hypothesis class never fits, so it has nothing to act on -- which matches the two
censuses in arc_scored_path_lever_harness.py finding it fits 0 of 25 and 1 of 15
public games. UNINTERPRETABLE_NOT_FITTED, not a null. Not recorded as evidence
about the lever's value, because it is not evidence about that.

THREE CASES NOW, CHECKED BEFORE HOLD, because they carry different instructions:

  identical arms, no counter moved   UNINTERPRETABLE_NO_EFFECT -- the flag never
                                     resolved. A WIRING result.
  identical arms, counters moved     UNINTERPRETABLE_FIRED_NO_EFFECT -- wired and
                                     running; read the counters to separate
                                     "fitted, nothing to do" from "never fitted".
  anything else                      the existing regression / HOLD / promote path

Both checks are fully general and need no per-lever knowledge: one diffs the
outcome rows, the other diffs whatever `*_diagnostics()` blocks the rows carry.

Scored rows now carry `fire_counters` -- 27 diagnostics blocks on a real run,
covering hazard pruning, frontier discipline, HUD masking, navigation, curiosity,
the reward machine and more. Collected by scanning the live object, not from a
maintained lever list: a hand-written list goes stale the next time a lever lands,
and a silently missing counter is precisely the false null this prevents. A
diagnostics method that raises records its error instead of losing the row.

Also fixes an older test that tripped the suite's 500MB memory guard by importing
the real solver kit; stubbed through sys.modules like its neighbours.

35 tests. Mutation-checked: deleting the no-effect branch turns all three new
verdict tests red, and each reverts to the misleading HOLD.
